292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (The wireframes were designed to improve visibility of internal projects by introducing an initial dashboard that visualises project timelines, task ownership, and dependencies across teams. By mapping projects and personnel in a structured interface, project managers can quickly identify overlapping workstreams and critical dependencies.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 161 0 R
/E (This structure begins to explore how tasks and responsibilities could be more easily reassigned if personnel changes occur, helping reduce potential disruptions and support project continuity. As early wireframes, the layout focuses on establishing a clear and accessible structure for visualising project progress, dependencies, and task ownership. These concepts will continue to be refined and iterated on to better support project managers in aligning tasks with strategic initiatives and making informed decisions.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
